{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00082",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Hi there, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.22,
      "end_seconds": 10.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Okay, of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.79,
      "end_seconds": 16.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Doctor, it's red scaly patches on my elbows. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.26,
      "end_seconds": 19.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.7,
      "end_seconds": 22.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "It's been going on for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.86,
      "end_seconds": 27.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Alright, how bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.27,
      "end_seconds": 29.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.12,
      "end_seconds": 32.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.35,
      "end_seconds": 40.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Pitted nails goes along with it, most of the time. The pitted nails? That's been for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.46,
      "end_seconds": 45.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.32,
      "end_seconds": 48.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.25,
      "end_seconds": 54.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Any eye redness or weeping at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.16,
      "end_seconds": 59.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Yeah, no, no eye redness or weeping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.47,
      "end_seconds": 63.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.03,
      "end_seconds": 77.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.97,
      "text": "Um, not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.87,
      "end_seconds": 85.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Right, what about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.23,
      "end_seconds": 95.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.36,
      "end_seconds": 105.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.43,
      "end_seconds": 109.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Oh, mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.84,
      "end_seconds": 114.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.22,
      "end_seconds": 117.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.21,
      "end_seconds": 123.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.47,
      "end_seconds": 132.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "I take metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.86,
      "end_seconds": 139.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Just to be sure I've got this right, the metformin, what dose was that again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.65,
      "end_seconds": 142.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "500 milligrams, like I said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.82,
      "end_seconds": 146.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.96,
      "end_seconds": 152.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I mean, I had cataract surgery on my right eye last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.48,
      "end_seconds": 164.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.03,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.73,
      "end_seconds": 167.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 167.88,
      "end_seconds": 175.38,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse is 69 beats a minute, respiratory rate 14. Pressure 112 over 77, temperature 36.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.7,
      "end_seconds": 177.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.5,
      "end_seconds": 180.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.06,
      "end_seconds": 183.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Of course, um, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.74,
      "end_seconds": 195.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.38,
      "end_seconds": 199.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.68,
      "end_seconds": 201.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.94,
      "end_seconds": 233.26,
      "duration_seconds": 22.32,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: My working impression is plaque psoriasis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had red scaly patches on your elbows for two years, moderate, and no eye redness or weeping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.22,
      "end_seconds": 235.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.47,
      "end_seconds": 251.67,
      "duration_seconds": 15.2,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.32,
      "end_seconds": 255.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Thank you, um, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.69,
      "end_seconds": 269.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for baseline before treatment. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'll start you on calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day, for four weeks. It's for psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.08,
      "end_seconds": 273.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Alright, uh, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.83,
      "end_seconds": 287.56,
      "duration_seconds": 13.73,
      "text": "A little sunlight helps psoriasis, but avoid sunburn. Moisturise often. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.25,
      "end_seconds": 290.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.73,
      "end_seconds": 294.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.52,
      "end_seconds": 302.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.69,
      "end_seconds": 307.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.57,
      "end_seconds": 316.38,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "So, I take the calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.01,
      "end_seconds": 320.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.62,
      "end_seconds": 323.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.12,
      "end_seconds": 326.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}